{"name":"Shrimp Boat","hex":"#f5be9d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shrimp boat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boat used for shrimp fishing.","A marker placed beside a blip on the radar screen, used by air traffic control to indicate a specific aircraft."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrimp_boat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shrimp Boat","blocks":[{"text":"Shrimp Boat was an American rock band formed in Chicago, Illinois in 1987. After the band dissolved in 1993, Sam Prekop and Eric Claridge formed The Sea and Cake. Ian Schneller and Tom Jasek went on to form Falstaff. Schneller's experience with the band would also lead him to create Specimen Products."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrimp_Boat","wikidata":"Q7504003"},{"title":"Shrimp","blocks":[{"text":"A shrimp is a common name typically used for crustaceans with an elongated body and a primarily swimming mode of locomotion. The name usually refers to decapods belonging to the Caridea or Dendrobranchiata, although some crustaceans outside this order are also referred to as \"shrimp\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Palaemon_serratus_Croazia.jpg/330px-Palaemon_serratus_Croazia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrimp","wikidata":"Q1517781"},{"title":"Boat","blocks":[{"text":"A boat is a watercraft of a large range of types and sizes, but generally smaller than a ship, which is distinguished by its larger size or capacity, its shape, or its ability to carry boats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Motorboat_at_Kankaria_lake.JPG/330px-Motorboat_at_Kankaria_lake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat","wikidata":"Q35872"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg/50